  "security": {
    "red": "tmp/p8/native-media-lifetime-run-bb/provenance-red.log",
    "pendingRed": "tmp/p8/native-media-lifetime-run-bb/pending-red.log",
    "mechanism": "Historical authority requires the actual PinnedHistoryMediaLease instance, the identical LocalMediaStore and a WeakSet member reference decoded from a historical source block of that pin. Reference metadata/content IDs alone grant no authority. Tail admission has its own typed source owner, propagated per block through the tail codec; scoped store release retires those owners before removing reservations. Unknown references use reserveAndReadVerified.",
    "lifetime": "History membership is weak and does not retain raw rows or enumerate all historical IDs. Pending admission registry holds only active scoped owner objects/content-ID scalars, not IContent/text. Its aggregate capacity is not a measured acceptance result.",
    "tailSemantics": "The existing bounded caller pending input is encoded in JournalTailSource. Its per-block admissions array carries owner references only, not raw rows/text or a second encoded-tail cache. Reading a source unit transfers that owner to the decoded immutable reference via a WeakMap. Owners belong to scoped live store reservations, survive history clear independently of obsolete historical ownership, and retire before reservation removal. The two cases cover previouslyOwned=false/true. Aggregate owner-registry capacity remains unmeasured.",
    "failureSemantics": "Unknown, cloned, fake-lease and cross-store inputs do not acquire historical authority. They take the existing verified reserve/read path in the resolver store. Blob verification failures propagate as RequestMediaResolutionError with their original cause; there is no catch-and-fallback read. Public readReserved has no new authorization flag/default and retains its documented already-reserved caller contract."
  },
